  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">USAID-Africa Small Grants</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to strengthen capacity to reduce bushmeat off take in and around key protected areas in Eastern Africa through a network of organizations and individuals working collaboratively to mobilize resources, share information, set priorities, and apply solutions. As a cooperative agreement between WCS and the USFWS, the project will catalyze action and guide activities to curtail illegal hunting and trade in bushmeat by developing a network (Bushmeat-free Eastern Africa Network, BEAN) of institutions, organizations, and individuals working together to resolve the problem of unsustainable bushmeat exploitation, and strengthen capacity for bushmeat monitoring in countries of Eastern Africa. USFWS will provide guidance, technical expertise, and financial support to BEAN. WCS-will provide technical support to the BEAN, oversee implementation of BEAN activities, and facilitate grant management and reporting obligations. BEAN will be implemented by a Director based at WCS-Uganda country program offices in Kampala reporting directly to WCS New York, USFWS, the BEAN Team, and to key partners within the region.</narrative>
  </description>
